WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.399 --> 00:00:04.232
- Hello Believe Nation.

00:00:04.232 --> 00:00:05.791
I am Evan Carmichael.

00:00:05.791 --> 00:00:08.077
My one word is believe and
I believe that entrepreneurs

00:00:08.077 --> 00:00:10.655
will solve all the major
problems of the world.

00:00:10.655 --> 00:00:12.210
So to help you on your journey,

00:00:12.210 --> 00:00:13.789
I'm going to share today the seven ways

00:00:13.789 --> 00:00:16.390
that smart people stay calm.

00:00:16.390 --> 00:00:17.806
And as always guys, as you're listening,

00:00:17.806 --> 00:00:19.664
if you here something that
really resonates with you,

00:00:19.664 --> 00:00:21.522
please leave it in the comments below

00:00:21.522 --> 00:00:24.099
and put quotes around it so
other people can be inspired.

00:00:24.099 --> 00:00:26.421
And the more you write
it down for yourself,

00:00:26.421 --> 00:00:29.004
the more likely it's going
to stick in here as well.

00:00:29.004 --> 00:00:29.837
Enjoy.

00:00:30.848 --> 00:00:32.062
- [Distorted Voice] Nine.

00:00:32.062 --> 00:00:32.895
Eight.

00:00:34.093 --> 00:00:38.176
(electronic hiphop instrumental)

00:00:41.477 --> 00:00:43.218
Rule number on is have a schedule.

00:00:43.218 --> 00:00:45.819
One of the things that
really helped me stay calm

00:00:45.819 --> 00:00:47.700
with all the things that were
happening in my business,

00:00:47.700 --> 00:00:50.161
was to have a schedule and
I know that there's a time

00:00:50.161 --> 00:00:53.458
for the thing that is causing an issue.

00:00:53.458 --> 00:00:56.013
And so for example,
Tuesday is my YouTube day.

00:00:56.013 --> 00:00:58.288
It's when I review all
the videos from my team.

00:00:58.288 --> 00:00:59.867
It's when I answer any questions,

00:00:59.867 --> 00:01:01.214
when I do setups for collaborations,

00:01:01.214 --> 00:01:02.259
when I'm doing the research.

00:01:02.259 --> 00:01:04.883
Anything basically YouTube
related except for filming,

00:01:04.883 --> 00:01:06.345
I do on a Tuesday.

00:01:06.345 --> 00:01:09.225
And so whenever I get
emails during the week,

00:01:09.225 --> 00:01:12.197
I get questions, I get
proposals, I get ideas.

00:01:12.197 --> 00:01:15.819
I review a video that then
spawns another creation.

00:01:15.819 --> 00:01:17.189
I have a place.

00:01:17.189 --> 00:01:19.349
I put it in my folder
and I know on Tuesday,

00:01:19.349 --> 00:01:21.346
I'm going to have time to go and do it

00:01:21.346 --> 00:01:23.784
and I think often times,
when we don't have time

00:01:23.784 --> 00:01:25.711
to figure it out and we
try to rush to solve it,

00:01:25.711 --> 00:01:27.777
it creates chaos, it creates stress,

00:01:27.777 --> 00:01:29.798
but knowing that you have
a place in your calendar

00:01:29.798 --> 00:01:32.177
to be able to do it,
for me at least, creates

00:01:32.177 --> 00:01:34.010
a great sense of calm.

00:01:37.553 --> 00:01:39.852
Number two is create a no-crisis business.

00:01:39.852 --> 00:01:41.500
This is a huge thing I'm a
fan of as an entrepreneur.

00:01:41.500 --> 00:01:45.167
I hate having to deal
with crisis, crisises.

00:01:46.005 --> 00:01:47.050
Crises?

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:49.163
I hate having to deal
with crises in the moment.

00:01:49.163 --> 00:01:51.021
I hate having a crisis business

00:01:51.021 --> 00:01:53.250
and so it's the reason
why I don't use the phone.

00:01:53.250 --> 00:01:54.922
Because what happens
when you have a phone?

00:01:54.922 --> 00:01:55.920
People call you.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:57.824
People call you with what
they think is an emergency

00:01:57.824 --> 00:02:00.564
but it's really they're
use for your time, right?

00:02:00.564 --> 00:02:02.863
It's their agenda for your
time instead of you saying

00:02:02.863 --> 00:02:05.092
I'm protecting my time and
I'm focusing on the things

00:02:05.092 --> 00:02:06.439
that really matter to me.

00:02:06.439 --> 00:02:08.830
And so, sometimes this means
you have to fire clients.

00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:10.734
You know, if I look at my main business,

00:02:10.734 --> 00:02:13.985
most brands who approach me
with a deal, I don't work with.

00:02:13.985 --> 00:02:16.354
Some of them just have
the wrong intentions,

00:02:16.354 --> 00:02:18.583
but some of them are just too needy.

00:02:18.583 --> 00:02:22.600
If you need me to be on
call 24-7 for your project

00:02:22.600 --> 00:02:24.109
to be a success,

00:02:24.109 --> 00:02:25.595
we're not going to work well together.

00:02:25.595 --> 00:02:27.128
That deal is not going to happen.

00:02:27.128 --> 00:02:29.589
Because I want to create
a no-crisis business

00:02:29.589 --> 00:02:32.886
and sometimes that means
you lose opportunities.

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:36.300
Sometimes that means that I
will miss media opportunities

00:02:36.300 --> 00:02:38.784
as an example because the
reporter's on a tight deadline

00:02:38.784 --> 00:02:40.479
and needs an answer by 4:00 today

00:02:40.479 --> 00:02:42.128
and I didn't even get the email

00:02:42.128 --> 00:02:44.287
until two o'clock the next day.

00:02:44.287 --> 00:02:47.004
Sometimes, that happens but you
have to be willing to let go

00:02:47.004 --> 00:02:48.769
of the good to go for the great.

00:02:48.769 --> 00:02:51.973
I'm using that time with
intention to focus on big,

00:02:51.973 --> 00:02:54.643
most important projects for my company,

00:02:54.643 --> 00:02:56.571
as opposed to only
dealing with little fire

00:02:56.571 --> 00:02:58.311
after little fire, after little fire.

00:02:58.311 --> 00:03:02.478
So as much as possible,
create a no-crisis business.

00:03:04.465 --> 00:03:06.207
Number three is close
your eyes and breathe.

00:03:06.207 --> 00:03:09.202
This sounds like a
pretty basic one but just

00:03:09.202 --> 00:03:11.780
reminding yourself that this is stressful.

00:03:11.780 --> 00:03:13.893
I'm going to breathe.

00:03:13.893 --> 00:03:15.565
I'm going to close my eyes.

00:03:15.565 --> 00:03:16.888
I'm going to relax.

00:03:16.888 --> 00:03:18.513
And things start to get better.

00:03:18.513 --> 00:03:21.207
Why do people go outside for a smoke?

00:03:21.207 --> 00:03:24.644
The nicotine helps but
it's also the breathing.

00:03:24.644 --> 00:03:27.523
And so if there's a
reminder on your calendar

00:03:27.523 --> 00:03:30.193
or something on your desktop background

00:03:30.193 --> 00:03:32.515
or whenever you feel that
stress coming on board,

00:03:32.515 --> 00:03:37.342
just reminding yourself,
I'm going to close my eyes.

00:03:37.342 --> 00:03:39.896
I'm going to take a
couple of deep breaths.

00:03:39.896 --> 00:03:43.896
I'm going to instantly feel
a little bit more calm.

00:03:45.515 --> 00:03:48.511
- So rule number four
is to have perspective.

00:03:48.511 --> 00:03:52.226
I think a lot of the times,
we get really focused

00:03:52.226 --> 00:03:53.944
on the nitty gritty of things,

00:03:53.944 --> 00:03:55.360
of things that are happening.

00:03:55.360 --> 00:03:57.125
You have emails coming through.

00:03:57.125 --> 00:03:59.145
You have telephone calls coming through.

00:03:59.145 --> 00:04:02.559
And we lose perspective
on what's important.

00:04:02.559 --> 00:04:07.249
So just last night, I was
ready to teach my Zumba class.

00:04:07.249 --> 00:04:10.105
I had my laptop ready,
everything was ready to go.

00:04:10.105 --> 00:04:11.220
I have my playlist.

00:04:11.220 --> 00:04:14.215
Everything is going as planned.

00:04:14.215 --> 00:04:18.382
10 minutes before my class
starts, my laptop shuts down.

00:04:21.413 --> 00:04:24.037
It just shuts down completely
and I started to panic

00:04:24.037 --> 00:04:26.197
and I couldn't turn it back on

00:04:26.197 --> 00:04:29.935
and immediately my thought was, oh my God,

00:04:29.935 --> 00:04:32.280
this happens to me all the time.

00:04:32.280 --> 00:04:34.881
Why does technology hate me so much?

00:04:34.881 --> 00:04:36.065
This has happened before.

00:04:36.065 --> 00:04:37.505
Many times.

00:04:37.505 --> 00:04:39.037
And then I started replaying

00:04:39.037 --> 00:04:40.407
all these weird things happening,

00:04:40.407 --> 00:04:42.938
like what if the girls
come in and I don't have

00:04:42.938 --> 00:04:45.353
the right playlist and then what do I do?

00:04:45.353 --> 00:04:46.723
What if I forget everything?

00:04:46.723 --> 00:04:48.186
What if I have no music?

00:04:48.186 --> 00:04:51.413
Oh God, do I go on
YouTube to download music.

00:04:51.413 --> 00:04:52.412
What is it?

00:04:52.412 --> 00:04:55.082
And I just started spiraling
and spiraling out of control

00:04:55.082 --> 00:04:59.656
and I felt a physiological
change in my body.

00:04:59.656 --> 00:05:03.000
I started turning really red and I felt

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.788
a sickness come over my stomach.

00:05:04.788 --> 00:05:05.949
I'm like oh gosh.

00:05:05.949 --> 00:05:07.435
This is anxiety.

00:05:07.435 --> 00:05:08.268
It's happening again.

00:05:08.268 --> 00:05:09.804
I'm getting anxious.

00:05:09.804 --> 00:05:13.751
And at that point, I took five minutes.

00:05:13.751 --> 00:05:17.428
I was like okay, I'm going
to give myself five minutes.

00:05:17.428 --> 00:05:18.774
I'm going to go in the back room

00:05:18.774 --> 00:05:21.236
and put things in perspective.

00:05:21.236 --> 00:05:22.211
It's a laptop.

00:05:22.211 --> 00:05:23.044
It's fine.

00:05:24.045 --> 00:05:25.740
It shut down, it's okay.

00:05:25.740 --> 00:05:29.293
I have another playlist on my phone.

00:05:29.293 --> 00:05:31.476
Yes, it's an old playlist
and I haven't done it since

00:05:31.476 --> 00:05:34.982
a year ago, but I still have a playlist.

00:05:34.982 --> 00:05:36.979
It's going to be fine.

00:05:36.979 --> 00:05:40.531
What's important is that
I have a group of students

00:05:40.531 --> 00:05:42.993
coming in with giant
smiles on their faces,

00:05:42.993 --> 00:05:45.129
wanting to do Zumba,

00:05:45.129 --> 00:05:47.172
want to get a nice workout.

00:05:47.172 --> 00:05:50.493
And want an environment that
is suportive and encouraging

00:05:50.493 --> 00:05:53.860
and I want them to feel
like they could love

00:05:53.860 --> 00:05:55.508
all of themselves.

00:05:55.508 --> 00:05:58.875
And me concerned about a
laptop or how technology's

00:05:58.875 --> 00:06:02.706
always after me and
nothing can ever get done

00:06:02.706 --> 00:06:04.657
because technology hates me,

00:06:04.657 --> 00:06:06.863
is not going to help my situation.

00:06:06.863 --> 00:06:10.207
So that five minutes, I calmed down.

00:06:10.207 --> 00:06:13.736
I put things in perspective
and five minutes later

00:06:13.736 --> 00:06:16.244
I found my old playlist.

00:06:16.244 --> 00:06:17.498
I played it.

00:06:17.498 --> 00:06:20.772
It wasn't ideal but it
was still an amazing class

00:06:20.772 --> 00:06:23.233
and everyone left really, really happy.

00:06:23.233 --> 00:06:25.601
So next time you feel like things are

00:06:25.601 --> 00:06:28.086
spiraling out of control,

00:06:28.086 --> 00:06:31.174
and you can't keep focus
and things are going wrong,

00:06:31.174 --> 00:06:35.091
just remember to put
everything in perspective.

00:06:38.210 --> 00:06:40.044
Number five is change your environment.

00:06:40.044 --> 00:06:42.250
So sometimes, just getting
up and going for a walk

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:43.713
really helps.

00:06:43.713 --> 00:06:45.826
I would find myself sometimes
getting stressed out

00:06:45.826 --> 00:06:48.148
at my old office and
especially on a nice day,

00:06:48.148 --> 00:06:51.515
I would spend 15 and
just go for a quick walk,

00:06:51.515 --> 00:06:52.513
clear my head.

00:06:52.513 --> 00:06:54.928
I really actually found that
helpful between switching tasks

00:06:54.928 --> 00:06:58.365
so if I had to go from writing
something really intense,

00:06:58.365 --> 00:07:00.780
that I had a 90-minute chunk to work on,

00:07:00.780 --> 00:07:03.171
and then I had to switch
to some other task,

00:07:03.171 --> 00:07:06.004
I would use that 15
minutes to clear my head,

00:07:06.004 --> 00:07:08.280
to just change my environment
and to set myself up

00:07:08.280 --> 00:07:10.532
to have success for
that next chunk of time.

00:07:10.532 --> 00:07:13.365
I find that sometimes it's the
people right in front of you

00:07:13.365 --> 00:07:15.269
or the environment that triggers you

00:07:15.269 --> 00:07:17.335
and just going for a walk and changing it

00:07:17.335 --> 00:07:20.252
can help bring you a sense of calm.

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:24.789
Number six is remember your why.

00:07:24.789 --> 00:07:27.181
Another thing I find really
helpful is remembering

00:07:27.181 --> 00:07:29.294
what I'm doing, why is this so important?

00:07:29.294 --> 00:07:30.640
Who am I trying to help?

00:07:30.640 --> 00:07:31.639
What's my mission?

00:07:31.639 --> 00:07:33.822
And so, if you're dealing
with some little stress

00:07:33.822 --> 00:07:36.190
that might be overwhelming in the moment,

00:07:36.190 --> 00:07:39.673
thinking about I'm
doing this thing because

00:07:39.673 --> 00:07:41.577
I wanted to help entrepreneurs,

00:07:41.577 --> 00:07:43.249
because my work matters.

00:07:43.249 --> 00:07:45.524
Because people leave
comments on all these videos

00:07:45.524 --> 00:07:48.357
and say how important a lot
of these videos are to them

00:07:48.357 --> 00:07:50.238
to stay motivated, to give them ideas

00:07:50.238 --> 00:07:52.072
to continue to build amazing things.

00:07:52.072 --> 00:07:56.345
And so, the stress of one
hater or a video not being

00:07:56.345 --> 00:07:59.526
ready on time or having to
switch around the schedule,

00:07:59.526 --> 00:08:02.382
those kinds of things
that can happen are small

00:08:02.382 --> 00:08:05.563
in comparison to the why of
what I'm trying to accomplish

00:08:05.563 --> 00:08:09.069
and keeping that focus and
whenever I'm kind of stressed out,

00:08:09.069 --> 00:08:11.066
remembering back to, why am I doing this?

00:08:11.066 --> 00:08:12.390
Why is this so important to me?

00:08:12.390 --> 00:08:16.140
Helps put those other
things not seem so big.

00:08:18.892 --> 00:08:21.190
And number seven is meditate.

00:08:21.190 --> 00:08:22.653
And I put this at number seven

00:08:22.653 --> 00:08:24.116
because I don't really meditate.

00:08:24.116 --> 00:08:25.927
I've never found a way to
really make it work for me,

00:08:25.927 --> 00:08:28.319
but it works for other
people so I had to include it

00:08:28.319 --> 00:08:29.549
on the list.

00:08:29.549 --> 00:08:31.593
For whatever reason, I've really wanted

00:08:31.593 --> 00:08:32.800
to learn to meditate.

00:08:32.800 --> 00:08:35.029
I've been on and off with
meditation for, I don't know,

00:08:35.029 --> 00:08:36.446
at least a decade.

00:08:36.446 --> 00:08:37.955
I just don't feel the benefit of it.

00:08:37.955 --> 00:08:39.650
I really want to though.

00:08:39.650 --> 00:08:41.368
I remember we went to
this Tony Robbins event

00:08:41.368 --> 00:08:44.364
a month or two ago in California.

00:08:44.364 --> 00:08:46.523
And they had this meditation guy come on

00:08:46.523 --> 00:08:48.683
and we were supposed to meditate.

00:08:48.683 --> 00:08:50.981
We're supposed to feel this
ball of energy between us

00:08:50.981 --> 00:08:53.071
and he was like, how many
of you can feel the ball?

00:08:53.071 --> 00:08:54.906
And (grumbling) I don't feel the ball.

00:08:54.906 --> 00:08:57.019
Where's the ball, where's the ball?

00:08:57.019 --> 00:08:58.180
I can't feel the ball.

00:08:58.180 --> 00:08:59.013
(laughing)

00:08:59.013 --> 00:09:01.536
I'm getting stressed out
trying to feel the ball.

00:09:01.536 --> 00:09:03.446
And then the next exercise,
you had to stand up

00:09:03.446 --> 00:09:05.571
and put your hand over somebody's
head and feel the energy

00:09:05.571 --> 00:09:06.973
field over the head.

00:09:06.973 --> 00:09:08.366
And I can't feel the energy field.

00:09:08.366 --> 00:09:09.443
How many of you guys
feel the energy field?

00:09:09.443 --> 00:09:10.650
Everybody shoots up their hand.

00:09:10.650 --> 00:09:11.997
And I'm like I can't
feel the energy field.

00:09:11.997 --> 00:09:13.460
So I don't know why.

00:09:13.460 --> 00:09:16.572
I think maybe in general,
I'm just pretty calm.

00:09:16.572 --> 00:09:18.522
I don't get stressed out that easily,

00:09:18.522 --> 00:09:21.169
but I'm going to add it on the list

00:09:21.169 --> 00:09:23.143
and hopefully maybe you guys will give me

00:09:23.143 --> 00:09:25.233
a resource that I can use,

00:09:25.233 --> 00:09:27.647
finally the resource
that will click with me

00:09:27.647 --> 00:09:29.482
so that meditation can be

00:09:29.482 --> 00:09:31.548
an important part of my daily routine.

00:09:31.548 --> 00:09:33.058
So that's my take on the seven ways

00:09:33.058 --> 00:09:34.613
that smart people stay calm.

00:09:34.613 --> 00:09:36.169
I'd love to know, what did you guys think?

00:09:36.169 --> 00:09:39.281
Which way was most relevant,
impactful, valuable to you?

00:09:39.281 --> 00:09:40.813
Leave it down in the comments below.

00:09:40.813 --> 00:09:43.158
Also, is there any eight,
nine, 10 that I missed

00:09:43.158 --> 00:09:45.364
that you want to add to the
list that really helped you,

00:09:45.364 --> 00:09:47.361
please share it because I think it'll help

00:09:47.361 --> 00:09:49.962
a lot of entrepreneurs who are
watching this video as well.

00:09:49.962 --> 00:09:51.285
So thank you guys again for watching.

00:09:51.285 --> 00:09:52.446
I believe in you.

00:09:52.446 --> 00:09:54.025
I hope you continue to believe in yourself

00:09:54.025 --> 00:09:56.045
and whatever your one word is.

00:09:56.045 --> 00:09:58.462
Much love, I'll see you soon.

